uperf-linux-rev (0.1.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship an audited SM8550 reference energy curve and power budgets derived
    from Uperf v3's sdm8g2 configuration.
  * Reproduce the reference sparse control OPPs, absolute energy-cost path,
    load-aware energy bucket, and one-step 0.9/1.1 package-cap feedback.
  * Preserve Android burst and dynamic cross-cluster efficiency semantics.
  * Enable the energy governor on the exact 3+4+1 SM8550 CPU topology while
    retaining Linux hardware, administrator, thermal, and recovery caps.
  * Drop the incomplete SM8750 profile, which has no current energy model.
  * Remove legacy planners, old configuration importers, and recovery-journal
    upgrade paths; accept only the current contracts.
  * Replace the version-1 D-Bus compatibility surface with the exact-match
    `org.uperflinux.Daemon2` API and one current decision-trace contract.
  * Keep the GNOME reporter off Mutter's untyped presentation signal while
    retaining focus, render-lifecycle, and display-power reporting.
  * Keep Android-derived values explicitly classified as reference data, not
    Linux rail measurements.

 -- uperf-linux contributors <noreply@example.invalid>  Sat, 01 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800

uperf-linux-rev (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add PolicyKit-authorized service enable and start controls to the GUI.
  * Add English and Simplified Chinese GUI localization.
  * Ship the GUI edition as a complete alternative to the headless package.
  * Fix a GUI capability refresh loop after the daemon first connects.
  * Add an eight-core SM8750 device profile.
  * Make device support JSON-driven with automatic exact profile matching,
    logical CPU groups, and directory-wide packaging.

